From 0d6ec9d374986dd5fb386a82c27ed8008045ca06 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 04:50:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] rename: Class -> type, Object -> object (snake_case
 stdlib doctrine)

the two hierarchy roots join the builtin classes' lowercase convention
(str/num/bool/array/map/function/nil/coro, and now object + type):
- the seeds table: 'object' (the root singleton), 'type' (the metaclass)
- the interned spellings in vm_init_singletons
- the one internal error message that named the root
- doc comments across src, and the five tests that used the old names

object is the root every hierarchy funnels into (isinstance(x, object)
is true for everything); type is the class of every class value
(classof(num) === type, the one self-loop classof(type) === type).
print output follows the names: <class object>, <class type>.
425/425 on plain, threaded, asan, aggressive-gc.
